          <span class="hint">{f.s3.emailHint}</span>
        </div>
        {/* No contact_method radio here, deliberately — and the reason is now
            stronger than when this was written. It used to be a collision to
            avoid: interactions.js bound a global handler on that radio group
            and set phone.required behind syncRequired()'s back, so the two
            would have fought over this field on every re-render. That handler
            (initContactPhone) was deleted in section 10 along with the order
            pages whose markup fed it, so the collision is now impossible rather
            than merely dodged. What remains is the design argument on its own
            merits: a plainly optional phone line asks for less and says the
            same thing. Re-adding the radio would mean re-deciding that, not
            just re-adding a field. */}
        <div class="field">
          <label for="pl-phone">{f.s3.phone} <span class="pl-opt">{f.optional}</span></label>
