      {/* The capacity gate, stated before anyone commits — which is why it now
          sits here rather than after </form>. Below the button it exists to
          reassure, it was a footnote to a decision already taken; and being
          outside the wizard it also greeted a visitor on step 1, before they
          had committed to anything at all. Step 5 is the commitment, so this is
          where the promise belongs, immediately above the control that acts on
          it. On the no-JS path, where all five steps are the page, it lands in
          exactly the same place.

          This is the only place on a public page where the system palette
          appears — see the --signal comment in global.css. It is a statement of
          process, not a scarcity badge: the site never counts down slots it has
          not verified. */}
      <p class="gate-note"><strong>{c.gateLead}</strong> {c.gateBody}</p>

      {/* Always visible, including without JS — this is the control that posts
          the form on every path through the page, so it can never live inside
          .pl-nav. The back button beside it is live-only and hides itself when
          there are no steps to go back through. */}
      <div class="pl-submit-row">
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-ghost pl-back-inline" data-pl-back>{f.back}</button>
        <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" data-pl-submit>{f.s5.submit}</button>
      </div>
    </section>
  </form>
</div></section>

<!-- WHAT IS THE SAME IN BOTH -->
